      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Around 1912, the Enoch family from Fernwood organized Kokomo, establishing the community that would grow into a small Mississippi town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kokomo%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early Kokomo hosted a turpentine distillery, blacksmith shops, a café, barbershop, grocery stores, gristmills, and a pharmacy, reflecting its diverse 20th‑century economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
